export anchor WorkingWithPiton:
    base:
        Read piton.config.pi to find the source root, the entry, the output, the
        plugins and the adapters. Then read the entry and its index files to the
        anchors of the task. The compiled reference gives an overview. If it
        does not agree with the source, the source is correct.

        Read the related source before you change it. Do not edit generated
        output. This includes generated guidance files, skill, command and agent
        files, renderer output, and files in .piton/manifest.json. Make each
        change in the .pi source, then build again.

        Open a reference only when the work needs it. Use piton reach to find
        what a change can affect. Use piton slice to read only the spec that one
        anchor or property needs.

        Make the smallest change that does the task. Use the conventions of the
        files near it. Then run piton format and piton check, and fix each
        problem in the source. Run piton build and read the diff of the
        generated files. Report each compiler error and warning as it is, with
        its file. Do not report success that the compiler did not show.
